// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5995 Add 4 detection rules for LLM and MCP attack surface
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5995
// Pull request author: ipunithgowda
// Change: new rule
// Title: Modification Of MCP Or Claude Configuration File - Linux
// Sigma ID: 89216c0a-8aca-43c1-a74b-b99adf8a2b56
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Punith Gowda (Network Intelligence)
// Date: 2026-05-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1546
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects writes to Claude Code or Claude Desktop configuration files where MCP server definitions
//   live. Files include .claude.json, ~/.claude/settings.json,
//   ~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json, and standalone mcp.json files. An attacker who can
//   write a new MCP server entry into these files gains arbitrary tool execution the next time the
//   agent loads, which is a stealthy persistence and command-and-control vector.
// False positives:
//   - Claude Code itself (runs as a node process) writing settings; covered by the filter but worth tuning per fleet (path of node binary varies)
//   - Configuration management tooling (Ansible, Chef, Puppet) deploying organisation-approved MCP server entries
//   - Backup or sync agents (rclone, restic, Dropbox client) restoring user dotfiles
// References:
//   - https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/concepts/architecture
//   - https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/settings
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1546/
//   - https://owasp.org/www-project-mcp-top-10/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/58c8781964014aba73b404e32ceafbb27d6668c8/rules-emerging-threats/2026/AI/file_event_lnx_mcp_config_file_modification.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/.claude.json" or FolderPath endswith "/.claude/settings.json" or FolderPath endswith "/.claude/settings.local.json" or FolderPath endswith "/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json" or FolderPath endswith "/mcp.json" or FolderPath endswith "/.cursor/mcp.json" or FolderPath endswith "/.continue/config.json") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/claude" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/cursor" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/node")))
